              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then recommends approve, reject, or request-info, with reasons, for a human admin to decide.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve one.\n\nThe project is at the offline-evals stage. On 31 test cases:\n- **Local 9B model:** approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without a human fell from 27% to 0%.\n- **Claude Haiku 5.5 (chosen for deployment):** 86% accuracy vs 71% for the local model, and 1% of fraud approved vs 8%. It escalates more cases to a human, and costs about $0.002 per review.\n\nIt's built with TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP."
              }
            ]
